course: dictionary
lesson: 1540
title: Chain: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word chain is a good example. «Toad is dragged off in chains, shrieking, across the market-place» means metal rings joined together, because you cannot be dragged in a chain of ideas or a chain of islands.
explain: Now look at «Venice held a chain of ports and islands along the Adriatic». Here chain means a row of things joined or following one another. Ask yourself: could I swap in the word row and still make sense? Yes, so this meaning fits.
explain: Some words link to a meaning you already know. «Wild hermit crabs sometimes queue by size and swap shells one after another» shows a chain of steps, where each crab moves into the shell left by the next. The sentence tells you the idea of a chain is a series of things following one another.
fact: A chain is a row of metal rings, called links, joined together.
fact: A chain can also be a row of things joined or following one another, like a chain of islands or a food chain.
fact: A chain is a group of shops or hotels with the same name, called a chain store or a chain hotel.
fact: To chain something means to tie it up with a chain, as in «Toad is dragged off in chains».
fact: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if it still makes sense, you probably have the right one.
exercise: «Toad is dragged off in chains, shrieking, across the market-place.» What are the chains here? | Shops with the same name | *Metal rings joined together, used to tie someone up | Sweet cakes shaped like rings | Long lines of people waiting for food
exercise: «Wild hermit crabs... swap shells one after another» is called a vacancy chain. What does this chain show? | A crab with a shell made of gold | A shop in the market-place | *A series of steps, each one following the last | Crabs fighting over food in the sea
exercise: Which phrase from the lessons means a group of shops with the same name? | paper chain | *chain store | food chain | bike chain
test: «Venice held a chain of ports and islands along the Adriatic.» What does chain mean in this sentence? | A shop with the same name | Metal rings used to hold a ship | To tie up with a chain | *A row of things joined or following one another
test: «An anchor... the weight of its chain helps hold the ship.» What does the chain do in this sentence? | Turns the ship into a castle | Makes the ship go faster | Melts in the sea | *Helps hold the ship in place
exam: Which sentence uses chain to mean tying something up with metal rings? | «Wild hermit crabs sometimes queue by size and swap shells.» | «Venice held a chain of ports and islands along the Adriatic.» | *«Toad is dragged off in chains, shrieking, across the market-place.» | «Leave a bike out in the rain all winter and its chain turns orange-brown.»
